            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="BOS02" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>William</forename>
                        <surname>Bosville</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1745-07-21">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1813-12-16"/>
                    <occupation>society host</occupation>
                    <occupation>reformer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Bosville was a society host who held daily dinners on weekdays for guests such as <persName key="TOO01">John Horne Tooke</persName>, 
      <persName key="BUR02">Francis Burdett</persName>, and and <persName key="EST01">Charles Este</persName>. He was a great 
    supporter of <persName key="TOO01">Horne Tooke</persName> and donated £1000 to <persName key="COB01">William Cobbett</persName> 
      when he was in prison 1810-12. He was one of the founding members of the Friends of the People.</p>
                    </note>
